From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:23:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmt6797: keep the core off LE

On the Gemini this controller sets the LE bit in its features, but its supported
commands list none of the basic LE commands. Octets 25 to 28 are all zero, and
LE Set Event Mask is refused with status 0x20. The core treats that as fatal, so
the device could not come up.

Clear the LE bit in the Read Local Features reply, so the core never starts its LE
setup. Which mask bit is refused, and whether LE can work at all, stays open.
Classic Bluetooth, which A2DP uses, needs none of it.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
index a625c1d3d..68bf9e201 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
+#include <linux/unaligned.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <linux/soc/mediatek/mt6797-stp.h>
 #include <net/bluetooth/bluetooth.h>
@@ -41,6 +42,18 @@ struct btmt6797 {
 	struct work_struct rx_work, error_work;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The controller sets the LE bit, but lists no basic LE command and refuses LE Set
+ * Event Mask, which fails the core's init. Only classic Bluetooth is offered.
+ */
+static void btmt6797_hide_le(struct sk_buff *skb, unsigned char type)
+{
+	/* Event, length, credits, opcode, status, then the eight feature bytes. */
+	if (type == HCI_EVENT_PKT && skb->len == 14 && skb->data[0] == HCI_EV_CMD_COMPLETE &&
+	    get_unaligned_le16(skb->data + 3) == HCI_OP_READ_LOCAL_FEATURES)
+		skb->data[6 + 4] &= ~LMP_LE;
+}
+
 static int btmt6797_emit(void *context, unsigned char type, const unsigned char *data,
 			 unsigned int length)
 {
@@ -52,6 +65,7 @@ static int btmt6797_emit(void *context, unsigned char type, const unsigned char
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	hci_skb_pkt_type(skb) = type;
 	skb_put_data(skb, data, length);
+	btmt6797_hide_le(skb, type);
 	skb_queue_tail(&bt->rx, skb);
 	return 0;
 }
